<p>Packer is a platform that introduces travellers with spare luggage space to senders who need something carried abroad. <strong>We do not inspect, handle, transport, or take possession of any item ourselves.</strong> Every handover happens directly and in person between a traveller and a sender, and the agreement to carry a specific item — along with full legal responsibility for it — is between those two people, not Packer.</p>

<h3>What can never be sent or carried</h3>
<p>It is strictly forbidden to send, request, offer to carry, or carry through Packer any item that is illegal, restricted, or banned by:</p>
<ul>
    <li>the customs or border-control authority of the country of origin or destination,</li>
    <li>the civil aviation authority governing the flight (e.g. PCAA, TSA, EASA, or the equivalent for that route), or</li>
    <li>airport or airline security regulations for that route.</li>
</ul>
<p>This includes — without limitation — illegal drugs or narcotics, weapons, firearms or ammunition, explosives, flammable or otherwise hazardous materials, counterfeit goods, and any other item prohibited under applicable law.</p>

<h3>The traveller's responsibility</h3>
<p>Before accepting or carrying anything, the <strong>traveller must personally inspect the item</strong> and confirm it matches what was described, and that they are satisfied it is legal and safe to carry on their trip. A traveller should always decline to carry anything they cannot verify, that arrives sealed against inspection, or that they have any doubt about.</p>

<h3>The sender's responsibility</h3>
<p>The <strong>sender is responsible for accurately describing</strong> the item being sent and for warranting that it is legal to send and to carry across the relevant border. An item must never be sealed in a way that prevents the traveller from inspecting it before departure.</p>

<h3>Our position</h3>
<p>Packer accepts <strong>no responsibility or liability whatsoever</strong> for any illegal, prohibited, or dangerous item sent or carried through the platform, or for any resulting consequence — including seizure, fines, detention, or criminal liability — for either the sender or the traveller involved. That responsibility rests entirely with the individuals who agreed to send and carry that item. Accounts found violating this policy may be suspended or permanently removed, and may be reported to the relevant customs, aviation, or law-enforcement authorities.</p>
